f on current iteration "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] = '1' or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1] = '1' let's increase the answer on one. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Asymptotic behavior of this solution — "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nm"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/problemset/problem/595/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"595B — Pasha and Phone"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's calculate the answer to every block separately from each other and multiply the answer to the previous blocks to the answer for current block."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the block with length equals to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" we can calculate the answer in the following way. Let for this block the number must be divided on "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and must not starts with digit "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then the answer for this block — the number of numbers containing exactly "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" digits and which divisible by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", subtract the number of numbers which have the first digit equals to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and containing exactly "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" digits and plus the number of numbers which have the first digit equals to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 (only if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" > 0) and containing exactly "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" digits."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Asymptotic behavior of this solution — "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" / "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/problemset/problem/594/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"594A — Warrior and Archer"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's sort the points by increasing "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" coordinate and work with sorted points array next."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's suppose that after optimal playing points numbered "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" < "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") are left. It's true that the first player didn't ban any of the points numbered "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" < "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" < "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", otherwise he could change his corresponding move to point "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" or point "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" (one could prove it doesn't depend on second player optimal moves) and change the optimal answer. It turns out that all the "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/73d422e03db01236bdb86d57d962cf848e5b05711d53a7a06c33d11375e15081.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" points banned by the first player have numbers outside of ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] segment, therefore "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/7050cd0bc6adb04039844acc26ea1ad126c1e305818da4ea1087512d7dbeee3d.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". We should notice that if the first player choosed any ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] for "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/05b92514e1e749f9b4a30a5d3fdb21360f0d457753a389904dbd450245186285.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", he could always make the final points numbers located inside this segment."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second player wants to make "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/05b92514e1e749f9b4a30a5d3fdb21360f0d457753a389904dbd450245186285.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" (he couldn't make less), what is equivalent if he always ban points inside final ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] segment (numbered "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" < "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" < "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). As soon as the second player doesn't know what segment first player have chosen after every of his moves, he must detect a point which satisfies him in every first player choice. It's true number of this point is the median of set of point numbers left (the odd number) after the first player move. The number of moves of the first player left is lesser by one than moves of the second player, so the first player later could ban some points from the left and some points from the right, except three middle points. Two of it (leftmost and rightmost ones) shouldn't be banned by the second player as soon as it could increase the size of banned points from the left (or from the right), but third middle point satisfies the second player in every first player choice. This way the second player always bans the point inside final point segment."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Thus the answer is the minimum between every of "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/a44e17090b42dcbec3fece9ce55edc285416edca5bc9fa91eb97d3a5ee1ec169.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" values."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/problemset/problem/594/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"594B — Max and Bike"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The main proposition to solve this problem — in the middle of every competition the sensor must be or in the top point of the wheel or in the bottom point of the wheel."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To calculate the answer we need to use binary search. If the center of the wheel moved on the distance "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the sensor moved on the distance "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"rsin"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" / "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), if the sensor was on the top point of the wheel in the middle, or on the distance "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"rsin"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" / "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), if the sensor was on the bottom point of the wheel in the middle, where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the radius of the wheel. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Asymptotic behavior of this solution — "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/b432c23d334e09047956d9416408ed84e7b9667078e9ccc415a7466093cfb2a5.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/problemset/problem/594/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"594С — Edo and Magnets"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's find the centers of every rectangle and multiple them of 2 (to make all coordinates integers).Then we need to by the rectangle door, which contains all dots, but the lengths of the sides of this door must be rounded up to the nearest integers. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now, let's delete the magnets from the door one by one, gradually the door will decrease. Obviously every time optimal to delete only dots, which owned to the sides of the rectangle. Let's brute 4"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" ways, how we will do delete the magnets. We will do it with helps of recursion, every time we will delete point with minimum or maximum value of the coordinates. If we will store 4 arrays (or 2 deques) we can do it with asymptotic "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(1). Such a solution works "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(4"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It can be easily shown that this algorithm delete always some number of the leftmost, rightmost, uppermost and lowermost points. So we can brute how "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" will distributed between this values and we can model the deleting with helps of 4 arrays. This solution has asymptotic behavior "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"4"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/problemset/problem/594/D"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"594D — REQ"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" "